# So Go already uses [::1]:9998 in the error message!
# The issue was just in how I format the error
# My formatNetError function was using ue.URL (the full URL) instead of extracting just the host

# Looking at the error: "Get \"http://localhost:9998/\": dial tcp [::1]:9998: connect: connection refused"
# 
# Original format: "error when dialing [::1]:9998: dial tcp [::1]:9998: connect: connection refused"
# My format should be: strip "Get URL: " prefix, then prepend "error when dialing HOST: "
# 
# But the HOST in original is "[::1]:9998" - the resolved IP
# In Go's error message, it says "dial tcp [::1]:9998: connect: connection refused"
# So the HOST part is "[::1]:9998"
# 
# The pattern: extract host from "dial tcp HOST: REASON", then format as "error when dialing HOST: FULL_ERR"
# where FULL_ERR = "dial tcp HOST: REASON"

# Let me extract the address from the error string
