# So for example.com, Go gives "context deadline exceeded" (HTTP-level timeout)
# But original shows "dialing to the given TCP address timed out"
# 
# This is because:
# - The original binary uses fasthttp which has separate DialTimeout and ReadTimeout
# - For external sites like example.com which are firewalled, the TCP connection times out
# - fasthttp shows "dialing to the given TCP address timed out" for dial timeout
# 
# In Go's http.Client, the Client.Timeout applies to the whole request
# including dial, header, body reading etc.
# But Go doesn't distinguish between "dial timeout" and "read timeout"
# unless you use a custom DialContext with a separate timeout
